section.exam-agreement__section
    h3.exam-agreement__section-title Target Audience
    div.exam-agreement__section-body Pulmonologists, critical care specialists, translational researchers, and clinicians.
section.exam-agreement__section
    h3.exam-agreement__section-title Learning Objectives for this Course
    div.exam-agreement__section-body
        p At the conclusion of this activity, learners should be able to:
        ul
            li Outline the components of a lung-protective ventilation strategy.
            li Understand the role of airway closure and measured pressures in acute respiratory distress syndrome.
            li Understand that strain changes happen despite constant tidal volumes if functional residual capacity changes.

section.exam-agreement__section
    h3.exam-agreement__section-title Credit Designation Statement
    div.exam-agreement__section-body
        p The American Thoracic Society is accredited by the Accreditation Council for Continuing Medical Education to provide continuing medical education for physicians.
        p The American Thoracic Society designates this educational activity for a maximum of 1 AMA PRA Category1 CreditTM. Physicians should only claim credit commensurate with the extent of their participation in the activity.
